  "body": "Found while fixing #1313.\n\n**What happens.** Since #1313 the mid-turn sweep (law c3) reads every tip position and every pose of a turn against the sampled stock columns (`crates/sim/src/verify/turn_cells.rs`). Its overhang backstop does not: stock hidden under a ledge (`Rest::hidden_in_annulus`, `crates/sim/src/verify/hidden.rs`) is still asked at 4 path stations x 5 turn fractions per band (`backstop_columns` in `crates/sim/src/verify/sweep.rs`), each at the one plane of that band's bottom. A holder or shank that swings through hidden stock between two of those poses gets no `SweepHit`.\n\n**Why it was left.** The hidden-stock law is sampled by its own statement (XY rings, one plane per ask) and slices the model once per distinct plane; covering a swept cell with its discs multiplies those slices, and a capsule/hull query needs a new entry point in `hidden.rs`. Bigger than the #1313 fix.\n\n**What still protects.** The finished part is the solid law's (it places the real pose). Only uncut stock under an overhang, met mid-turn, is exposed.\n\n**Expected.** The backstop bounds the same cells the column law reads (a swept query in `hidden.rs`, or a disc cover with a stated bound), with the slice count kept in budget.\n\nDone means: a turn whose band crosses hidden stock between two of the five sampled poses gets a `SweepHit`, pinned by a test that fails before the change; `overhang_laws` stays green; the slice count per move is stated.\n",
